    "description": "Several Interactivity API binding issues let a user with the Contributor role or above store cross-site scripting or a denial of service in post content: inherited property lookups that reach `innerHTML`, `__proto__` as a directive name, bindings to internal props or inherited methods, and `data-wp-style` writing into any resolved object.\r\n\r\nWordPress 7.1.4 has been released containing fixes for these vulnerabilities, and as a courtesy to users on older branches the fixes have been backported to all branches back to 6.4.\r\n\r\nDiscovered and responsibly disclosed by rekter0, Marcel Karlsson (whoismarcel), Jon Surrell and Alex Concha of the WordPress Security Team.",
